From: enuma-fix <enuma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] power: qcom: smb5: disable charger watchdog while USB input is suspended (unplug + deep-sleep reboot fix)

On Xiaomi Pad 5 Pro (elish/enuma) unplugging the USB cable while the screen
is off causes a silent hard reset ~64s later. Root cause: the PM8150B bark
watchdog is petted only by wdog_bark_irq_handler(), but the bark interrupt is
suppressed at the PMIC level whenever the USB input is suspended, so during
unplugged deep sleep the dog is never petted and eventually bites -> PMIC
reset. Disable the charger watchdog timer (WDOG_TIMER_EN_ON_PLUGIN_BIT |
BARK_WDOG_INT_EN_BIT in WD_CFG_REG) while the USB input is suspended and
restore it on plugin/resume. Native deep sleep and charging protection while
plugged are both preserved.

Signed-off-by: enuma-fix <enuma@local>
---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom/smb5-lib.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom/smb5-lib.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom/smb5-lib.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom/smb5-lib.c
@@ -775,6 +775,29 @@
 		smblib_err(chg, "Couldn't write %s to USBIN_SUSPEND_BIT rc=%d\n",
 			suspend ? "suspend" : "resume", rc);
 
+	/*
+	 * [PATCH] Unplug + deep-sleep watchdog fix (Xiaomi Pad 5 Pro / elish-enuma).
+	 *
+	 * The PM8150B bark watchdog is petted ONLY by wdog_bark_irq_handler(),
+	 * but the bark interrupt is suppressed at the PMIC level whenever the USB
+	 * input is suspended ("On USB suspend, WDOG IRQ stops triggering", see
+	 * smblib_handle_therm_regulation). On unplug the input is suspended, so the
+	 * AP never receives the bark interrupt and the dog is never petted; after
+	 * the bark+bite window the PMIC hard-resets the device (~64s after unplug
+	 * + screen-off). Disable the charger watchdog timer (and its bark
+	 * interrupt) while the USB input is suspended so it cannot bite during deep
+	 * sleep; restore it on plugin/resume. Charging protection while plugged is
+	 * unaffected because the input is then active and the bark keeps firing.
+	 */
+	{
+		int wd_rc = smblib_masked_write(chg, WD_CFG_REG,
+				WDOG_TIMER_EN_ON_PLUGIN_BIT | BARK_WDOG_INT_EN_BIT,
+				suspend ? 0 :
+				(WDOG_TIMER_EN_ON_PLUGIN_BIT | BARK_WDOG_INT_EN_BIT));
+		if (wd_rc < 0)
+			smblib_err(chg, "Couldn't %s charger watchdog rc=%d\n",
+				suspend ? "disable" : "enable", wd_rc);
+	}
 	if (!suspend)
 		vote(chg->icl_irq_disable_votable, USB_SUSPEND_VOTER,
 				false, 0);
